From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 20:16:51 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali-oneplus-iceland: skin trips at
 stock's 60/61 C

The skin thermistor (stock sys-therm-2, pmh0101_skin_therm) sits next to
the SoC and rises about 3 C per second under an all-core load. Its zone
ran the step-wise loop from 48 C and applied the deepest gear at 51 C.
Those two values are the battery-temperature steps of the vendor
framework's high-temperature protection, not limits for this sensor: on
the vendor kernel the zone has six passive trips (48, 49, 50, 60, 61 and
90 C, hysteresis 2 C) and no cooling map at all, and the throttling is
done in userspace on a shell temperature fitted from five sensors, in
which this thermistor weighs 0.18 to 0.43. That userspace policy (the
stock gear table: CPU, GPU, brightness and charging caps per gear) runs
on this tablet as iceland-thermal.

Move the kernel loop to the vendor's own trips 3 and 4 on the sensor:
the step-wise loop from 60 C and the deepest gear (cpufreq-cpu0 state
22 = 998400 kHz, cpufreq-cpu6 state 27 = 883200 kHz, GPU state 13 =
342 MHz) at 61 C. The hysteresis, the cooling maps and the 70 C
critical trip (the vendor's device shutdown temperature; its last
marker on this sensor is 90 C) are unchanged. The loop is now the
backstop under the userspace policy, as the vendor kernel's zones are.

Tested on the OnePlus Pad 4 (area-combo-39, the same trips on kernel
q53 with the policy daemon): the emulation walk acted at 60 / 61 C and
released, the policy followed the vendor table in 20 of 20 steps, and a
60 s all-core load did 40 % more work than with the 48 / 51 C loop
(area-combo-38: 281872 vs 202032 work chunks, 4446 vs 3131 chunks per
second in the last 30 s) with the skin thermistor peaking at 56.0 C.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts | 17 +++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
index de61a1a76ffa..1355c4cfe97f 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
@@ -2493,12 +2493,13 @@
 	};
 
 	/*
-	 * Skin. Stock marks this sensor (sys-therm-2) at 48, 49, 50, 60, 61 and 90 C and leaves the throttling to
-	 * its userspace thermal service; that service's high-temperature protection steps in at 48 C (out at 46),
-	 * protects at 51 C (out at 49) with the deepest gear of its table (CPU level 13 = 998400 / 883200 kHz,
-	 * GPU level 6 = 342 MHz) and shuts down at 70.0 C (odm sys_high_temp_protect, sys_thermal_control_config).
-	 * The same steps are done here in the kernel: from 48 C the step-wise governor throttles as far as needed,
-	 * down to that deepest gear at most; at 51 C the deepest gear applies at once; 70 C shuts down.
+	 * Skin thermistor, a fast hot spot next to the SoC. Stock marks this sensor (sys-therm-2) at 48, 49, 50,
+	 * 60, 61 and 90 C (hysteresis 2 C) without any cooling map: its throttling is done in userspace on a shell
+	 * temperature fitted from this sensor, the board, WLAN and charge-pump thermistors and the battery (here:
+	 * iceland-thermal). The kernel loop is the backstop under that policy, on stock's own trip temperatures:
+	 * from 60 C the step-wise governor throttles as far as needed, down to the deepest gear of stock's table at
+	 * most (CPU level 13 = 998400 / 883200 kHz, GPU level 6 = 342 MHz); at 61 C that gear applies at once;
+	 * 70 C (stock's shutdown temperature for the device) shuts down.
 	 * Cooling states: cpufreq-cpu0 22 = 998400 kHz, cpufreq-cpu6 27 = 883200 kHz, GPU 13 = 342 MHz.
 	 */
 	skin-thermal {
@@ -2508,13 +2509,13 @@
 
 		trips {
 			skin_alert0: skin-alert0 {
-				temperature = <48000>;
+				temperature = <60000>;
 				hysteresis = <2000>;
 				type = "passive";
 			};
 
 			skin_alert1: skin-alert1 {
-				temperature = <51000>;
+				temperature = <61000>;
 				hysteresis = <2000>;
 				type = "passive";
 			};
